<> EXPORT/IMPORT
if its random changesets between different repositories that are not connected to each other use hg export/import

hg export changeset > changeset.patch
hg export changeset + 1 > changeset+1.patch

keep in midn that the changesets shoudl each be in separate files. You can number them so at the receiving end they can be 
applied in the right order.

hg import changeset
hg import changeset+1


<> BUNDLE/UNBUNDLE for inter branch integrations
You can do a hg outgoing http://someotherrepo.com find out what changes are heading out.

Take the highest changelist thats your topChange

hg bundle -r topChange bundle.name http://someotherrepo.com

thats it pass bundle.name to the owner of this repo in whatever way you deem necessary. 
they can just hg unbundle bundle.name


<> BUNDLE/UNBUNDLE for cherry picking changes
You can do the following if you want to just create a bundle of changes from your repo

hg bundle -r highestChange --base lowestChangeYouWantIncludedMinusOne bundle.name

Thats it this new bundle can be transported around. 

AFAIK you cannot cherry pick changes using bundle/unbundle they need to be consecutive.

<> TRANSPLANT

hg transplant -s ./../mainrepo 10:16 

keep in mind theres a bug in transplant where it doesnt work if there are merge conflicts